Fertilizer-Pump licensing overview
Copyright (c) 2026 Paulus Handke

This repository contains works under different licenses. There is no single
repository-wide noncommercial restriction. The following grants cover only
original material for which Paulus Handke holds the relevant rights.

1. Firmware and its original build configuration
   GPL-3.0-only (GNU General Public License, version 3 only).
   Full text: LICENSES/GPL-3.0-only.txt
   Commercial use and distribution are permitted under the GPL. Hardware and
   documentation restrictions must not be imposed on this software.

2. Original hardware designs and manufacturing outputs
   CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 (Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0
   International).
   Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt
   Applies to copyright and similar rights in the protected design material.
   Commercial use of those rights requires separate permission. This is not a
   guarantee of control over physical manufacture or operation of hardware.

3. Original project documentation and illustrations
   CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 (Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0
   International).
   Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt
   Commercial use requires separate permission.

See LICENSING.md for file assignments, contribution and release requirements,
and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for third-party materials and unresolved provenance.
Third-party rights are not relicensed by this overview. Individual notices and
upstream licenses continue to apply, including to embedded library material.
License texts themselves retain their own copying terms.

The CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 standard text is unmodified. Its attribution, NonCommercial
and ShareAlike conditions apply as written. It does not require publication of
editable CAD source, and does not license patents, trademarks or design rights.
Creative Commons does not recommend its licenses for hardware; this project uses
the license for protected design files, without claiming comprehensive control
over physical products, independent designs or unprotected functional features.

Separate additional permission for paid fabrication: To the extent of Paulus
Handke's rights, a customer may give the design files to a paid fabrication or
assembly service solely to fulfill an order for the customer's otherwise
permitted noncommercial end use. The service may reproduce the necessary design
material and make and deliver the ordered items for that purpose. This grant
does not authorize independent commercial sales or other commercial exploitation,
does not override third-party rights, and imposes no restriction on rights
already granted by CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. It is an additional permission, not a change
to the standard license.

Additional permission for compliance notices: You may reproduce and distribute
this licensing overview, LICENSING.md, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, and the production
licensing instructions verbatim as needed to communicate or comply with license
terms, including alongside commercial firmware distributions. Preserve their
attribution. This does not grant commercial rights to other documentation or
hardware designs, or change any third-party license.

Commercial permission requests for the original hardware or documentation:
https://github.com/Handkep/Fertilizer-Pump/issues
An inquiry or lack of response is not permission. Only a separate written
agreement from the relevant rights holder grants additional rights.

This overview does not withdraw any rights validly granted for earlier copies.
